const absEN = [
  h1("Abstract"),
  body([new TextRun({ text: "The integrity of anti-corrosion coating on wind turbine towers directly determines their load-bearing capacity and service life. Coating defects such as inclusions, pinholes, scratches and contaminants must be located and repaired before delivery, while manual visual inspection suffers from low efficiency and inconsistent standards. Based on CoatingDet, a production-line dataset of 5,416 high-resolution images labeled with two classes (defect and particle), this thesis reproduces the YOLOv11n baseline under the official protocol and improves it against three weaknesses: accuracy collapse in the warm-color domain, defect-dust confusion, and small-object localization. The improvements include a CBAM attention module before the detection heads, a WIoUv3 bounding-box regression loss with a gradient-allocation clamp, and a grey-world white-balance plus widened hue-jitter input alignment strategy. Experiments show that CBAM raises mAP50 by " + delta("C_cbam", "A0", "val") + ", " + delta("C_cbam", "A0", "test_1") + " and " + delta("C_cbam", "A0", "test_2") + " points on the validation set and two cold-domain test sets respectively; the white-balance strategy reduces particle-to-defect false alarms on the warm test set from 175 to 13. Trained for 60 epochs, the baseline itself generalizes better across domains, but the attention model overfits the training color domain; the final model is therefore the CBAM configuration under the official 20-epoch schedule, whose mean mAP50 over the four domains reaches " + mean4("C_cbam") + "%, outperforming same-scale YOLOv5nu, YOLOv8n and YOLOv10n. An interactive web demo is also developed, and the failure of naive improvement stacking is analyzed mechanistically.", size: 24, font: { ascii: "Times New Roman" } })]),
  new Paragraph({ spacing: { before: 240 }, children: [new TextRun({ text: "Key words: ", bold: true, size: 24, font: { ascii: "Times New Roman" } }), new TextRun({ text: "wind turbine tower; coating defect detection; YOLOv11; attention mechanism; cross-domain generalization", size: 24, font: { ascii: "Times New Roman" } })] }),
];

